<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n298" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăcanthĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>from Acanthus</i>, a town in Macedonia: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 7, 41, § 85</span></i>
			.</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> †
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcanthus</span></b> ,
				i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκανθος</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The plant bear's-breech</i>, <i>bear's-foot</i>, or <i>brankursine</i>: Acanthus
			mollis, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 3, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 20</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id. G.
				4, 123</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 1, 649</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 22,
				22, 34, § 76 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Fem.</i>, <i>a thorny evergreen tree
				of Egypt</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2, 119</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2,
				56, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 24, 12, 66 sq.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
